<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1377" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesōn</span></b> , ŏnis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴσων</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Thessalian
			prince</i>, <i>brother of king Pelias</i>, <i>and father of Jason</i>, <i>who</i>,
				<i>according to fable</i>, <i>was in
				extreme old age transformed by the magic arts of Medea into a
				youth</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7, 2</span></i>.— Whence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesŏnĭdes</span></b> , ae, <i>patr. m.</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἰσονίδης</span>, <i>a male descendant of
				Æson</i>, i. e. <i>Jason</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				164</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phasias Aesoniden, Circe tenuisset Ulixem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					A. 2, 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mobilis Aesonide,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					H. 6, 109 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aesŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Æsonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heros,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Jason</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 156</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					H. 12, 134</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
